ow contamination-control procedures\&quot;, \&quot;Use approved leak-off/return tests\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Common-rail fuel can penetrate skin. Never search for leaks with hands.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 9, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Fuel Contamination &amp; Water Diagnosis\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Intermediate\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Fuel\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Sample fuel safely\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect separator/water sensor\&quot;, \&quot;Check filter condition\&quot;, \&quot;Identify gasoline/DEF/water contamination risk\&quot;, \&quot;Follow OEM contamination procedure\&quot;, \&quot;Replace/flush only as specified\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Contaminated high-pressure systems can require extensive component replacement.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 10, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;DPF Regeneration Diagnosis\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Aftertreatment\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Read soot/ash estimates and inhibit reasons\&quot;, \&quot;Check differential-pressure data\&quot;, \&quot;Verify exhaust-temperature sensors\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect for upstream engine faults\&quot;, \&quot;Determine passive/active/service regen status\&quot;, \&quot;Follow OEM stationary-regen conditions\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Forced regeneration can create extreme exhaust temperatures and fire risk.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 11, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;SCR / DEF System Diagnosis\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Aftertreatment\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Confirm DEF quality/level\&quot;, \&quot;Read inducement and dosing faults\&quot;, \&quot;Check temperature prerequisites\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect dosing system for crystallization/leaks\&quot;, \&quot;Review NOx sensor data\&quot;, \&quot;Run OEM functional tests\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;DEF faults are often system faults; avoid replacing NOx sensors without test evidence.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 12, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;EGR System Diagnosis\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Emissions\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Review commanded vs actual EGR\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect position feedback\&quot;, \&quot;Check differential-pressure/flow sensing\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect cooler and piping\&quot;, \&quot;Check intake deposits where serviceable\&quot;, \&quot;Verify related boost/airflow faults\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Allow hot EGR and cooling-system components to cool before service.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 13, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Cooling System Overheat\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Cooling\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Verify actual temperature\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect coolant level/condition cold\&quot;, \&quot;Check radiator/CAC debris\&quot;, \&quot;Verify fan command and engagement\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect thermostat/water-pump symptoms\&quot;, \&quot;Check for combustion/cooling-system cross-contamination\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Never remove a pressurized cooling-system cap while hot.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 14, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulic System Slow / Weak\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulics\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Confirm fluid level/condition\&quot;, \&quot;Check filter/restriction indicators\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect leaks and suction-side aeration\&quot;, \&quot;Measure pressure/flow with rated equipment\&quot;, \&quot;Compare pump command/displacement where applicable\&quot;, \&quot;Isolate circuit vs pump/system fault\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulic injection injuries are medical emergencies. Never use hands to find pinhole leaks.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 15, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulic Cylinder Drift\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulics\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Confirm load and safe blocking\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect external leakage\&quot;, \&quot;Check valve/load-holding circuit\&quot;, \&quot;Perform OEM-approved isolation test\&quot;, \&quot;Evaluate cylinder bypass vs control-valve leakage\&quot;, \&quot;Retest after repair\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Never rely on hydraulics alone to support raised equipment.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 16, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulic Hose &amp; Fitting Inspection\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Intermediate\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Hydraulics\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Depressurize and secure machine\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect abrasion, cracking, blistering and leaks\&quot;, \&quot;Check routing/bend radius\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect fittings and clamps\&quot;, \&quot;Match hose pressure/temperature/application rating\&quot;, \&quot;Clean system before reconnection\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Do not patch pressure hose. Replace with correctly rated assemblies.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 17, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;24V Starting &amp; Charging Diagnosis\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Electrical\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\&quot;Identify 12/24V architecture\&quot;, \&quot;Load-test batteries individually\&quot;, \&quot;Inspect series/parallel connections\&quot;, \&quot;Perform voltage-drop tests\&quot;, \&quot;Measure cranking voltage/current where appropriate\&quot;, \&quot;Test alternator output to OEM specification\&quot;], \&quot;safety\&quot;: \&quot;Disconnecting or shorting high-current battery circuits can cause burns and explosions.\&quot;}, {\&quot;id\&quot;: 18, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;CAN Bus / Sensor Fault Strategy\&quot;, \&quot;level\&quot;: \&quot;Advanced\&quot;, \&quot;system\&quot;: \&quot;Electrical / Controls\&quot;, \&quot;steps\&quot;: [\