pan&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Survey the site, roof condition, shading, service equipment, and usable array area.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Collect recent energy-use data and define the project goal: offset, resilience, or both.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Choose a preliminary system architecture: string inverter, optimizers, or microinverters.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Estimate array size and verify that the proposed layout respects access, setbacks, and local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create a one-line concept and equipment schedule before purchasing components.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Route permitting, utility-interconnection, structural, and electrical decisions through the applicable authority and qualified professionals.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-1\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;site survey, roof &amp;amp; shading assessment\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Design\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Site Survey, Roof &amp;amp; Shading Assessment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Design&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect roof age, covering, penetrations, framing clues, slope, orientation, and access.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Document obstructions such as vents, skylights, chimneys, parapets, and nearby trees.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record shading conditions across the proposed array area.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Measure usable roof planes from a safe position; do not improvise fall protection.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Photograph service equipment, meter, main panel, roof planes, and proposed equipment locations.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Flag structural uncertainty, damaged roofing, or unsafe access before design proceeds.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-2\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;pv module selection &amp;amp; array layout\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Design\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. PV Module Selection &amp;amp; Array Layout&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Design&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compare module electrical ratings, dimensions, connector type, warranty, and mounting compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lay out modules around roof geometry and required access areas.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Group modules logically for the selected inverter architecture.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check voltage/current design limits using manufacturer data and expected temperature conditions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Plan wire management so conductors remain supported and protected.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Freeze the layout only after structural, electrical, and permitting constraints are reconciled.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-3\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;string sizing &amp;amp; dc voltage design\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Electrical\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. String Sizing &amp;amp; DC Voltage Design&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Collect module Voc, Vmp, Isc, temperature coefficients, and inverter DC limits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Determine the cold-temperature condition required by the applicable design rules.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check maximum string open-circuit voltage against inverter/system limits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check operating voltage against the inverter MPPT window.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify current limits for parallel strings and input channels.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Document the final string map and do not substitute modules without recalculating the design.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-4\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;racking, flashing &amp;amp; roof attachment\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Roof\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Racking, Flashing &amp;amp; Roof Attachment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Roof&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm roof structure and approved attachment locations.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lay out attachment points to match the engineered or manufacturer-approved mounting plan.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use roof-compatible flashing/sealing methods and listed mounting components.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Install rails or rail-less mounts to specified alignment and torque.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Bond/ground mounting components as required by the listed system and applicable rules.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect every penetration and attachment before modules conceal the work.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-5\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;module installation &amp;amp; mechanical finish\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Roof\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. Module Installation &amp;amp; Mechanical Finish&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Roof&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stage modules using safe lifting methods rather than carrying panels up ladders.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify clamps, attachment zones, and fastener torque from manufacturer instructions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set modules without pinching conductors or damaging backsheets/connectors.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain planned gaps, alignment, and required access.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Secure conductors beneath the array with approved management hardware.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Perform a mechanical walkdown before electrical commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-6\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;dc wiring, connectors &amp;amp; cable management\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Electrical\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. DC Wiring, Connectors &amp;amp; Cable Management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify conductor type, rating, routing, and compatibility with the PV system.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use only compatible connector families and manufacturer-approved assembly tools/procedures.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Route conductors away from sharp edges, standing water, abrasion, and roof contact.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Support and protect wiring continuously beneath the array.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Label and identify circuits according to the approved design.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treat exposed PV conductors as energized whenever illuminated unless verified otherwise under the required safe-work procedure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-7\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;combiner boxes, ocpd &amp;amp; dc disconnects\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Electrical\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;8. Combiner Boxes, OCPD &amp;amp; DC Disconnects&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Determine whether the architecture requires combining, overcurrent protection, or dedicated disconnecting equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Match equipment voltage/current ratings to the engineered design.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Maintain polarity and circuit identification from array to equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Install listed equipment in approved locations with required working clearances.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Terminate conductors to manufacturer torque specifications.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify isolation/disconnect function before commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically 