ll&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify the authority having jurisdiction and electric utility before final design.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prepare required site plan, array layout, equipment data, and electrical one-line documentation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Include structural information and equipment listings where required.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Submit permit and interconnection applications before work that requires approval.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Resolve plan-review corrections without silently changing the field design.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Retain approved plans, inspection results, and utility authorization with project records.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-14\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;system labeling &amp;amp; documentation\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Commissioning\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;15. System Labeling &amp;amp; Documentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Commissioning&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div clas