nvironmental conditions without defeating safety barriers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use qualified service personnel for internal or energized diagnostics.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm normal operation and monitoring after corrective work.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-19\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;solar pv preventive maintenance &amp;amp; annual inspection\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Maintenance\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. Solar PV Preventive Maintenance &amp;amp; Annual Inspection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Maintenance&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review production history for unexplained decline or recurring faults.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect accessible modules, racking, wiring support, labels, enclosures, and visible roof conditions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check vegetation/shading changes and safe cleaning needs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review inverter and monitoring logs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Have qualified personnel address electrical defects, damaged connectors, or abnormal heating indications.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Update the maintenance record with observations, repairs, and production baseline.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Field rule:&lt;/b&gt; Solar PV can remain electrically energized in daylight, and rooftop work adds serious fall hazards. Follow the approved design, manufacturer instructions, adopted electrical/building/fire rules, utility requirements, and qualified-person restrictions.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;solar-20\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;footer&gt;Educational field reference. Not a permit, engineering plan, inspection approval, license, or substitute for qualified electrical/structural work.&lt;/footer&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;script&gt;\nlet currentCat='ALL';\nfunction toggleGuide(b){b.closest('.guide').classList.toggle('open')}\nfunction filterCat(c){currentCat=c;applyFilters()}\nfunction applyFilters(){\n let q=document.getElementById('search').value.toLowerCase();\n document.querySelectorAll('.guide').forEach(g=&gt;{g.style.display=((currentCat==='ALL'||g.dataset.cat===currentCat)&amp;&amp;g.dataset.title.includes(q))?'block':'none'})\n}\nfunction saveProgress(el){localStorage.setItem(el.dataset.id,el.checked?'1':'0');updateProgress()}\nfunction updateProgress(){\n let n=0;document.querySelectorAll('.done input').forEach(x=&gt;{if(x.checked)n++});\n document.getElementById('progress').textContent=n+'/20 Complete';\n}\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.done input').forEach(x=&gt;{x.checked=localStorage.getItem(x.dataset.id)==='1'});updateProgress();\n&lt;\/script&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&quot;}, {&quot;emoji&quot;: &quot;⚡🚗&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Electric Vehicles&quot;, &quot;file&quot;: &quot;tradestack-premium-electric-vehicles-v1.html&quot;, &quot;html&quot;: &quot;&lt;!doctype html&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset=\&quot;utf-8\&quot;&gt;&lt;meta name=\&quot;viewport\&quot; content=\&quot;width=device-width,initial-scale=1\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;title&gt;TradeStack Premium — Electric Vehicles v1&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#05070d;color:#edf3ff;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}.wrap{max-width:920px;margin:auto;padding:18px}\n.hero{padding:22px;border:1px solid #25324a;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#0a1020,#10192c);margin-bottom:14px}\n.brand{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:1.8px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#75d8ff}h1{margin:6px 0 4px}.sub{color:#aebbd0;line-height:1.5}\n.stats{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px}.stat,.tags span{background:#162138;border:1px solid #2a3a58;border-radius:999px;padding:7px 10px;font-size:13px}\ninput[type=search]{width:100%;padding:14px;border-radius:13px;border:1px solid #33435e;background:#0d1423;color:white;font-size:16px;margin:10px 0}\n.filters{display:flex;gap:7px;overflow:auto;padding:4px 0 12px}.filters button{white-space:nowrap;background:#101a2c;color:#dce8ff;border:1px solid #2b3b57;border-radius:999px;padding:8px 11px}\n.guide{border:1px solid #263550;background:#0b1220;border-radius:16px;margin:10px 0;overflow:hidden}.head{width:100%;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;text-align:left;background:none;color:white;border:0;padding:16px;font-size:15px}\n.head small{display:block;color:#7f93b5;margin-top:5px}.body{display:none;padding:0 16px 17px}.guide.open .body{display:block}.guide.open .chev{transform:rotate(45deg)}.tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin-bottom:14px}\nli{margin:9px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#d6dfed}.warn{background:#24120d;border:1px solid #6b2d1c;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;line-height:1.45;color:#ffd1c4}.done{display:block;margin-top:14px;padding:11px;background:#101a2c;border-radius:12px}\nfooter{color:#7f93b5;text-align:center;padding:24px 8px;font-size:12px}\n&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;wrap\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;section class=\&quot;hero\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;brand\&quot;&gt;TradeStack Premium&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;⚡🚗 Electric Vehicles&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;sub\&quot;&gt;20 advanced EV field guides covering charging, high-voltage safety, batteries, drivetrain, diagnostics, thermal systems, and inspection.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;stats\&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot;&gt;20 Guides&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot;&gt;Premium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot; id=\&quot;progress\&quot;&gt;0/20 Complete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;input id=\&quot;search\&quot; type=\&quot;search\&quot; placeholder=\&quot;Search EV guides…\&quot; oninput=\&quot;applyFilters()\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;filters\&quot;&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('ALL')\&quot;&gt;All&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Battery')\&quot;&gt;Battery&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Brakes')\&quot;&gt;Brakes&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Charging')\&quot;&gt;Charging&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Diagnostics')\&quot;&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Drivetrain')\&quot;&gt;Drivetrain&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Electrical')\&quot;&gt;Electrical&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('HVAC')\&quot;&gt;HVAC&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Inspection')\&quot;&gt;Inspection&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Safety')\&quot;&gt;Safety&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Thermal')\&quot;&gt;Thermal&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div id=\&quot;guides\&quot;&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;ev high-voltage safety fundamentals\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Safety\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. EV High-Voltage Safety Fundamentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Safety&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify the vehicle&amp;#x27;s high-voltage warning labels, service disconnects, battery location, and restricted zones.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify required PPE, insulated tools, CAT-rated meter requirements, and OEM shutdown procedure before service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Establish a controlled work area and prevent unauthorized access.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use the OEM-specified power-down sequence and required wait time before testing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Prove the meter on a known source before and after absence-of-voltage testing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not open sealed high-voltage components unless trained, authorized, and following the OEM repair procedure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-1\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;ev no-start / no-ready diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Diagnostics\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. EV No-Start / No-Ready Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm the symptom: no power, no READY state, intermittent READY, or immediate shutdown.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check 12V battery condition and low-voltage system health first.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scan all relevant control modules and save codes before clearing anything.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify charge state, key/immobilizer status, interlock faults, and thermal shutdown conditions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Follow OEM diagnostic trees before touching high-voltage components.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Escalate to qualified HV testing when faults point to battery, inverter, contactors, or isolation circuits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-2\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;12v battery &amp;amp; low-voltage system diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Electrical\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. 12V Battery &amp;amp; Low-Voltage System Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Yes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Measure resting and loaded 12V battery voltage using the correct test method.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect battery terminals, grounds, fuses, DC-DC charging behavior, and parasitic draw clues.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scan for undervoltage codes across multiple modules.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm the DC-DC converter supports the low-voltage system when the vehicle is in READY.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check for corrosion, loose grounds, or aftermarket accessories affecting wake/sleep cycles.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Replace or charge the 12V battery only after confirming it is actually the root cause.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-3\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;ev charging basics: level 1, level 2 &amp;amp; dc fast charging\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Charging\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. EV Charging Basics: Level 1, Level 2 &amp;amp; DC Fast Charging&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Charging&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Yes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify the connector standard and charging mode supported by the vehicle.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm EVSE ratings, branch-circuit requirements, and available electrical capacity.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Separate vehicle-side charging faults from EVSE or utility-side problems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Understand that AC charging uses the onboard charger while DC fast charging bypasses it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check charging schedules, thermal limits, battery state of charge, and software settings.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use manufacturer guidance before diagnosing connector, inlet, contactor, or isolation faults.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-4\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;level 2 home evse planning\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Charging\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Level 2 Home EVSE Planning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Charging&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Determine desired charging power based on vehicle capability and daily energy needs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Assess panel capacity, existing loads, breaker space, wire route, and installation location.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify local permit, inspection, grounding, GFCI, and load-calculation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Select listed EVSE compatible with the vehicle and installation environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Have qualified personnel complete panel/service work and final branch-circuit installation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Commission the EVSE and verify stable charging at the intended current.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-5\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;ev will not charge diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Diagnostics\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. EV Will Not Charge Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Test with a known-good charging station or alternate EVSE when possible.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check connector seating, charge-port damage, locking mechanism, and obvious contamination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review charge schedules, SOC limits, battery temperature, and fault messages.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scan onboard charger, battery-management, and charging-control modules.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect low-voltage support systems before condemning high-voltage hardware.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Escalate internal charger, battery, contactor, or isolation testing to qualified EV service personnel.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EV safety rule:&lt;/b&gt; High-voltage EV systems can remain hazardous even when the vehicle appears off. Use OEM shutdown procedures, rated PPE/test equipment, and qualified-person restrictions. Never bypass interlocks, contactors, insulation monitoring, or battery protections.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;ev-6\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;slow charging diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Diagnostics\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. Slow Charging Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;chev\&quot;&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compare requested charging power with vehicle, EVSE, and circuit limits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check battery temperature, state of