fd1c4}.done{display:block;margin-top:14px;padding:11px;background:#101a2c;border-radius:12px}footer{color:#7f93b5;text-align:center;padding:24px 8px;font-size:12px}&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;wrap\&quot;&gt;&lt;section class=\&quot;hero\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;brand\&quot;&gt;TradeStack Premium&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;🔋 Battery &amp; Backup Power&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;sub\&quot;&gt;20 advanced guides covering storage, inverters, transfer systems, hybrid backup, diagnostics, commissioning, and maintenance.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;stats\&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot;&gt;20 Guides&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot;&gt;Premium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=\&quot;stat\&quot; id=\&quot;progress\&quot;&gt;0/20 Complete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/section&gt;&lt;input id=\&quot;search\&quot; type=\&quot;search\&quot; placeholder=\&quot;Search Battery guides…\&quot; oninput=\&quot;applyFilters()\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;filters\&quot;&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('ALL')\&quot;&gt;All&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Battery')\&quot;&gt;Battery&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Commissioning')\&quot;&gt;Commissioning&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Controls')\&quot;&gt;Controls&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Design')\&quot;&gt;Design&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Diagnostics')\&quot;&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Electrical')\&quot;&gt;Electrical&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Hybrid')\&quot;&gt;Hybrid&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Maintenance')\&quot;&gt;Maintenance&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Planning')\&quot;&gt;Planning&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button onclick=\&quot;filterCat('Safety')\&quot;&gt;Safety&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;battery backup safety &amp;amp; system fundamentals\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Safety\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Battery Backup Safety &amp;amp; System Fundamentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Safety&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify battery chemistry, nominal DC voltage, inverter rating, disconnects, and emergency shutdown points.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Establish ventilation, fire-response, PPE, and restricted-access requirements for the equipment used.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treat battery conductors as capable of extremely high fault current even at comparatively low voltages.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Remove metal jewelry and use insulated tools where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Follow manufacturer shutdown and re-energization procedures before service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not work on damaged, swollen, leaking, smoking, or thermally unstable batteries outside an approved emergency procedure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-1\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;load assessment &amp;amp; critical-circuit planning\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Planning\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Load Assessment &amp;amp; Critical-Circuit Planning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Planning&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;List essential loads and separate must-run equipment from optional loads.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record watts, starting surge, duty cycle, and expected outage duration for each load.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Size the system for both energy capacity and peak power demand.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Account for inverter losses, reserve capacity, battery aging, and temperature effects.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify which circuits will be backed up and how they will be isolated from noncritical loads.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify that the planned system fits applicable electrical, building, fire, and utility requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-2\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;battery capacity, kwh &amp;amp; runtime estimation\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Planning\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Battery Capacity, kWh &amp;amp; Runtime Estimation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Planning&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;List essential loads and separate must-run equipment from optional loads.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record watts, starting surge, duty cycle, and expected outage duration for each load.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Size the system for both energy capacity and peak power demand.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Account for inverter losses, reserve capacity, battery aging, and temperature effects.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify which circuits will be backed up and how they will be isolated from noncritical loads.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify that the planned system fits applicable electrical, building, fire, and utility requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-3\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;inverter / charger selection\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;D