t;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify battery chemistry, nominal DC voltage, inverter rating, disconnects, and emergency shutdown points.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Establish ventilation, fire-response, PPE, and restricted-access requirements for the equipment used.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treat battery conductors as capable of extremely high fault current even at comparatively low voltages.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Remove metal jewelry and use insulated tools where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Follow manufacturer shutdown and re-energization procedures before service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not work on damaged, swollen, leaking, smoking, or thermally unstable batteries outside an approved emergency procedure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-18\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;system commissioning &amp;amp; backup test\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Commissioning\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;19. System Commissioning &amp;amp; Backup Test&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Commissioning&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm mechanical installation, labeling, clearances, protective devices, and wiring are complete.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify polarity, grounding/bonding, conductor torque, communications, and configuration before energizing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Follow manufacturer energization sequence and observe startup status.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Simulate a utility outage using the approved test method and verify intended critical loads remain powered.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check charging recovery, transfer back to utility, alarms, and shutdown functions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Save baseline voltage, current, temperature, runtime, and configuration data for future comparison.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-19\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;preventive maintenance &amp;amp; annual backup inspection\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Maintenance\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. Preventive Maintenance &amp;amp; Annual Backup Inspection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Maintenance&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review event logs, battery health, cycle count, state-of-charge behavior, and any recurring alarms.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect enclosures, ventilation, terminals, cables, disconnects, labels, and signs of heat or corrosion.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Test backup operation on the schedule recommended by the manufacturer.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Keep firmware/settings documentation and service records current.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Replace worn or failed batteries/components with approved equivalents.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Recalculate expected runtime when major loads or battery capacity change.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stored-energy rule:&lt;/b&gt; Battery systems can deliver enormous fault current, remain energized when the grid is off, and create fire/thermal hazards. Use approved disconnecting, overcurrent, grounding, ventilation, transfer, and emergency procedures. Service-panel, transfer-switch, and internal battery/inverter work belongs with qualified personnel.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;battery-20\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;footer&gt;Educational field reference. Follow manufacturer instructions and applicable electrical, building, fire, utility, battery, and workplace requirements.&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;let currentCat='ALL';function toggleGuide(b){b.closest('.guide').classList.toggle('open')}function filt