 Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Observe the property during or soon after rainfall when possible and map where water originates, travels, ponds, and exits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check roof discharge, grading, hardscape slopes, low spots, soil erosion, retaining walls, and foundation perimeter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record elevations or relative fall with appropriate leveling tools rather than relying only on appearance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Separate surface runoff, groundwater, plumbing leaks, irrigation leaks, and condensation before choosing a repair.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Photograph evidence such as staining, sediment, efflorescence, erosion, and vegetation changes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build the repair around the confirmed water source and a safe discharge point.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Water-management rule:&lt;/b&gt; Find the source before installing a drain or coating. Excavation, foundation work, retaining walls, hydrostatic pressure, electrical equipment near water, and deep below-grade waterproofing can require qualified contractors or engineering.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;dw-2\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;finish grading &amp;amp; positive drainage\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Site Drainage\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Finish Grading &amp;amp; Positive Drainage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Site Drainage&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ 