harge, gas, water, heat, pressure, and moving parts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Unplug equipment or use the approved disconnect/lockout method before disassembly.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify de-energization with an appropriate tester when electrical exposure is possible.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Protect floors and control water before disconnecting hoses or valves.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not bypass door switches, thermal devices, fuses, interlocks, grounding, or other safety systems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stop when the repair enters sealed refrigeration, gas, microwave high-voltage, or energized diagnostics beyond your qualification.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Appliance rule:&lt;/b&gt; Unplugging an appliance does not make every internal component harmless. Capacitors, gas systems, heating circuits, sharp sheet metal, moving parts, refrigerants, and microwave high-voltage systems require appropriate procedures and qualification.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;appliance-1\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;multimeter basics for appliance diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Electrical\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Multimeter Basics for Appliance Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review the wiring diagram and identify the component and expected test condition before measuring.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Disconnect power for resistance/continuity tests unless the procedure explicitly requires otherwise.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm meter leads, function, range, and instrument rating before contact.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Measure components in a way that avoids false readings through parallel circuits when applicable.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Compare results with manufacturer service information rather than guessing from continuity alone.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reconnect grounds, covers, strain reliefs, and protective devices before return to service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Appliance rule:&lt;/b&gt; Unplugging an appliance does not make every internal component harmless. Capacitors, gas systems, heating circuits, sharp sheet metal, moving parts, refrigerants, and microwave high-voltage systems require appropriate procedures and qualification.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;appliance-2\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;refrigerator not cooling diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Refrigeration\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Refrigerator Not Cooling Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Refrigeration&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm actual compartment temperatures and customer symptoms before replacing parts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check door sealing, airflow blockage, condenser cleanliness, fan operation, frost