. Garbage Disposal Jam / No-Start Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Kitchen&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Disconnect power before reaching into the disposal or working underneath it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm the sink is clear and inspect for a simple foreign-object jam without placing hands into the grinding chamber.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use the manufacturer-provided turning method/tool if the unit supports manual freeing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check the reset only after the jam/overload cause is addressed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect mounting, drain connections, and leaks before restoring service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Electrical connection, damaged housing, or persistent motor faults should be handled by qualified service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Appliance rule:&lt;/b&gt; Unplugging an appliance does not make every internal component harmless. Capacitors, gas systems, heating circuits, sharp sheet metal, moving parts, refrigerants, and microwave high-voltage systems require appropriate procedures and qualification.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;appliance-18\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;appliance leak diagnosis\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Diagnostics\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;19. Appliance Leak Diagnosis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Determine whether the leak occurs during fill, wash, drain, heat, defrost, or only when idle.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Trace water upward from the lowest wet point to hoses, valves, pumps, seals, drains, pans, and supply connections.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Dry the area before controlled testing so new leakage is distinguishable from old water.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Correct loose routing, clogs, or approved serviceable seals/components as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not repeatedly operate an appliance that is leaking onto electrical parts or flooring.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Run a supervised test and inspect all disturbed connections.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Appliance rule:&lt;/b&gt; Unplugging an appliance does not make every internal component harmless. Capacitors, gas systems, heating circuits, sharp sheet metal, moving parts, refrigerants, and microwave high-voltage systems require appropriate procedures and qualification.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;appliance-19\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;pre-repair appliance inspection &amp;amp; repair-or-replace decision\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Inspection\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. Pre-Repair Appliance Inspection &amp;amp; Repair-or-Replace Decision&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Inspection&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Yes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Normal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Record model/serial information, age, symptoms, error codes, and prior repair history.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect cord/plug, hoses, cabinet, corrosion, leaks, unusual odors, heat damage, and mechanical condition.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Estimate parts, labor, downtime, and likely remaining appliance life.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Consider safety recalls or manufacturer service information when applicable.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Avoid expensive component replacement until the root fault is reasonably confirmed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Document the diagnosis and whether repair, professional service, or replacement is the sensible path.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Appliance rule:&lt;/b&gt; Unplugging an appliance does not make every internal component harmless. Capacitors, gas systems, heating circuits, sharp sheet metal, moving parts, refrigerants, and microwave high-voltage systems require appropriate procedures and qualification.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;appliance-20\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;footer&gt;Educational field reference. Manufacturer service information, electrical/gas requirements, refrigerant rules, and qualified service procedures control actual repairs.&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;let currentCat='ALL';function toggleGuide(b){b.closest('.guide').classList.toggle('open')}function filterCat(c){currentCat=c;applyFilters()}function applyFilters(){let q=document.getElementById('search').value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('.guide').forEach(g=&gt;g.style.display=((currentCat==='ALL'||g.dataset.