sture after correction to confirm the problem stays corrected.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;IAQ rule:&lt;/b&gt; Source control comes first. Ventilation and filtration cannot make an active combustion hazard, major moisture source, or hazardous contaminant harmless. CO alarms, fuel odors, combustion spillage, and significant contamination require immediate appropriate response.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;iaq-17\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;combustion appliance backdrafting awareness\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Combustion\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;18. Combustion Appliance Backdrafting Awareness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Combustion&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ensure functioning carbon-monoxide alarms are present as required and respond to any alarm as a safety event.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inspect for obvious vent disconnection, corrosion, soot, blocked combustion-air openings, or abnormal appliance conditions without dismantling fuel equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not intentionally create unsafe depressurization or defeat appliance safeties.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Combustion analysis, gas pressure, venting repair, and spillage testing require appropriate qualification and instruments.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If CO exposure is suspected, move occupants to fresh air and follow emergency guidance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not return suspect equipment to service until the hazard is properly evaluated.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;IAQ rule:&lt;/b&gt; Source control comes first. Ventilation and filtration cannot make an active combustion hazard, major moisture source, or hazardous contaminant harmless. CO alarms, fuel odors, combustion spillage, and significant contamination require immediate appropriate response.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;iaq-18\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;co₂, co &amp;amp; indoor pollutant monitoring basics\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Monitoring\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;19. CO₂, CO &amp;amp; Indoor Pollutant Monitoring Basics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Monitoring&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Choose a monitor for the pollutant/question rather than assuming one consumer sensor measures everything.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Place sensors according to manufacturer instructions and away from misleading localized conditions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use trends over time for CO₂, humidity, particles, or VOC indicators where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Treat carbon monoxide separately as an acute life-safety hazard requiring listed alarms and immediate response.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Recognize that low-cost VOC/particle sensors may be useful for trends but are not laboratory identification tools.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use professional sampling when a health, legal, occupational, or remediation decision requires validated measurements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;IAQ rule:&lt;/b&gt; Source control comes first. Ventilation and filtration cannot make an active combustion hazard, major moisture source, or hazardous contaminant harmless. CO alarms, fuel odors, combustion spillage, and significant contamination require immediate appropriate response.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;iaq-19\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;final ventilation &amp;amp; iaq inspection\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Inspection\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. Final Ventilation &amp;amp; IAQ Inspection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Inspection&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Walk outdoor-air intakes, exhausts, occupied spaces, filters, accessible ducts, moisture-prone areas, and ventilation equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify fans and ventilation controls operate as intended.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Check filter condition, airflow complaints, condensation, odors, visible moisture damage, and blocked grilles.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Confirm exhausts terminate appropriately and intakes are not drawing from obvious pollutant sources.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Review monitor trends or commissioning readings when available.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create a risk-ranked punch 