fety, planning &amp;amp; existing-condition survey\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Planning\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Remodel Safety, Planning &amp;amp; Existing-Condition Survey&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Planning&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Yes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $ Low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Document existing dimensions, plumbing, electrical, ventilation, structure, finishes, and known damage before demolition.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Define the finished layout and verify fixture/appliance clearances, door swings, cabinet depths, and working space.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify permit, inspection, licensed-trade, and manufacturer requirements before ordering materials.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate rough-in dimensions from actual selected fixtures and appliances, not generic assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sequence structural, plumbing, electrical, ventilation, waterproofing, cabinetry, tile, and finish work logically.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Photograph concealed conditions and rough-ins before walls and floors are closed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remodel rule:&lt;/b&gt; A beautiful finish cannot rescue bad rough-in work hiding behind it. Structural changes, new electrical circuits, regulated plumbing/gas work, and complex waterproofing must follow applicable permits, codes, manufacturer systems, and qualified-trade requirements.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;remodel-1\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;