nning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Electrical&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Pro Recommended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$$ High&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Map lighting, receptacles, appliances, controls, ventilation equipment, and dedicated-load requirements.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Identify required GFCI/AFCI and other protection under applicable electrical rules.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate box heights and locations with cabinets, mirrors, tile, backsplashes, and appliances.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not bury junctions or create inaccessible electrical connections.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use qualified electrical personnel for new circuits, panel work, and regulated wiring.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Function-test protection devices and equipment after finish installation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remodel rule:&lt;/b&gt; A beautiful finish cannot rescue bad rough-in work hiding behind it. Structural changes, new electrical circuits, regulated plumbing/gas work, and complex waterproofing must follow applicable permits, codes, manufacturer systems, and qualified-trade requirements.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;remodel-8\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;bathroom exhaust &amp;amp; moisture-control planning\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Ventilation\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. Bathroom Exhaust &amp;amp; Moisture-Control Planning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Ventilation&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY: Caution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Difficulty: Advanced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cost: $$ Medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Safety: High Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Field workflow&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Estimate moisture/odor load and select appropriately sized exhaust equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Plan a short, smooth duct path terminating outdoors at an appropriate location.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate fan, duct, electrical, ceiling, roof/wall penetration, and exterior termination before finishes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Insulate or control condensation on ducts where conditions require it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Verify actual fan operation and airflow after installation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not discharge bathroom exhaust into attics or concealed building cavities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;warn\&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remodel rule:&lt;/b&gt; A beautiful finish cannot rescue bad rough-in work hiding behind it. Structural changes, new electrical circuits, regulated plumbing/gas work, and complex waterproofing must follow applicable permits, codes, manufacturer systems, and qualified-trade requirements.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;label class=\&quot;done\&quot;&gt;&lt;input type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; data-id=\&quot;remodel-9\&quot; onchange=\&quot;saveProgress(this)\&quot;&gt; Mark guide complete&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/article&gt;&lt;article class=\&quot;guide\&quot; data-title=\&quot;shower pan &amp;amp; drainage system fundamentals\&quot; data-cat=\&quot;Waterproofing\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;button class=\&quot;head\&quot; onclick=\&quot;toggleGuide(this)\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;10. Shower Pan &amp;amp; Drainage System Fundamentals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;small&gt;Waterproofing&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;＋&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;div class=\&quot;body\&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=\&quot;tags\&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;DIY